; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR BIG CLOCK  -  seven-segment digits from the Elf2K's DS12887   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; NEEDS THE $07 RTC OPCODE (V0061.35).
;
; The time as six big seven-segment digits (HH:MM:SS, 24-hour) made of reverse-video
; blocks across the middle of the screen; the day of the week on the line below, and the
; date ("October 2, 2026") on the line below that. Plain VT100: cursor addressing and
; reverse video only; nothing scrolls. Each second only the rows of a digit that changed
; are sent (the day and date only when the date changes).
;
; S sets the clock: the date as YYYY-MM-DD, the time as HH:MM:SS (24-hour); the firmware
; checks every field and writes nothing if one is wrong. Q or ESC quits.
; Warns if the clock is stopped, its battery flat, or it is in 12-hour mode.
;
; Not in the web Simulator: it has no RTC.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/bigclock_verify.py, V0061.34 + RTC-07): ALL PASS 2026-10-03 (digits read back off a strict VT100 screen): the Elf2K BIOS's binary mode, 15:48:59 Fri 2 Oct 2026 -> ticking; at most 325 bytes a second (mean 140); midnight on New Year's Eve -> Friday, January 1, 2027; S sets 2026-07-04 09:05:00 (chip written, Saturday); 2026-02-30 refused with nothing written; Enter cancels; a never-set chip warns; Q clears and restores the cursor; a rerun without reloading.
;
; 347 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

